From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/25] apklayer: pi-mutex-attr

Audio's real priority-inheritance mutex must translate its attribute object too; falling back to glibc writes over the mapped bionic pointer.

apklayer patch: step 10 of the former scripts/patch-bionic-translation.sh (see docs/PATCHES.md), patch 0010 of patches/bionic_translation.
---
 pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c b/pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c
index 58af132..0e33b76 100644
--- a/pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c
+++ b/pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c
@@ -429,6 +429,19 @@ int bionic_pthread_mutexattr_settype(bionic_mutexattr_t *attr, int type)
 	return pthread_mutexattr_settype(attr->glibc, type);
 }
 
+/* apklayer patch: preserve the mapped attribute ABI for audio PI mutexes. */
+int bionic_pthread_mutexattr_setprotocol(bionic_mutexattr_t *attr, int protocol)
+{
+    assert(attr && IS_MAPPED(attr));
+    return pthread_mutexattr_setprotocol(attr->glibc, protocol);
+}
+
+int bionic_pthread_mutexattr_getprotocol(const bionic_mutexattr_t *attr, int *protocol)
+{
+    assert(attr && IS_MAPPED(attr));
+    return pthread_mutexattr_getprotocol(attr->glibc, protocol);
+}
+
 int bionic_pthread_mutexattr_destroy(bionic_mutexattr_t *attr)
 {
 	assert(attr);
